cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Empirical study of US IPO first-day returns, 2019-2024"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lyonn
    family-names: Lie
    alias: leeyawnnn
repository-code: "https://github.com/leeyawnnn/ipo_underpricing_model"
abstract: >-
  Measurement study of first-day returns on US IPOs listed between 2019 and
  2024. Combines SEC EDGAR S-1/F-1 prospectus text scored with the
  Loughran-McDonald dictionary, SEC-assigned SIC sectors, Carter-Manaster
  underwriter reputation ranks from Jay Ritter, and split-corrected first-day
  closes from Yahoo Finance. Reports a hypothesis-test family with
  multiple-testing correction and out-of-sample model performance against
  constant baselines.
keywords:
  - initial public offerings
  - underpricing
  - textual analysis
  - Loughran-McDonald
  - SEC EDGAR
  - empirical finance
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
